usage: unitron asm [-h] [-o OUTPUT] [-I INCLUDE] [-D DEFINE] [--origin ORIGIN] [--size SIZE] [--fill FILL] [--place SECTION=ADDR] [--lcf FILE] [--data-base DATA_BASE] [--code-base CODE_BASE] [--no-link] [--no-mpp] [--strict] [--sym SYM] [-H] [-O LEVEL] [-M FILE] [-MG] [-MP] [-MT TARGET] sources [sources ...]

assemble (and link) asm900 sources into a raw image

positional arguments:
  sources	one module per file

options:
  -h, --help	show this help message and exit
  -o, --output OUTPUT
  -I, --include INCLUDE
  -D, --define DEFINE
  --origin ORIGIN	image start address (default: lowest code/romdata byte)
  --size SIZE	image size (default: up to the highest byte)
  --fill FILL	byte for gaps (default 0xFF)
  --place SECTION=ADDR
  --lcf FILE	place relocatable sections with a Toshiba link command file (docs/lcf.md)
  --data-base DATA_BASE	first address for data sections
  --code-base CODE_BASE	first address for code/romdata
  --no-link	check one module; externs stay unresolved
  --no-mpp	skip the macro preprocessor
  --strict	enforce asm900's include limits
  --sym SYM	write a symbol file (address name)
  -H	also accept suffixed numbers (1234H, 101B, 17O/17Q, 99D), as asm900 -H
  -O LEVEL	j/cal: -O1 (default) shortest jr/jrl/jp and calr/call; -O0 always jp/call (asm900 -O)
  -M FILE	write a make dependency file (- = stdout) listing every file read; without -o only the includes are read
  -MG	with -M: a missing include file is listed (it will be generated), not an error
  -MP	with -M: an empty rule for each include file, so make doesn't fail when one is deleted
  -MT TARGET	with -M: the rule's target (default: the -o file); may be repeated
